---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const example = `version: 1
vars: { migrations_dir: db/migrations }
exceptions:
  - { rule: migrations-via-generator, path: 'db/migrations/0000_bootstrap.sql', enforce: warn }
rules:
  - id: migrations-via-generator
    description: 'DB migrations must be produced by \`make migrate\`.'
    scope: both
    tags: [db, generative]
    when:
      all: [{ path: '\${migrations_dir}/**' }]
      any: [{ diff_not_contains: '! Generated by make migrate' }]
    enforce: block
  - id: no-protected-edits
    scope: hook
    when:
      any:
        - { path: 'README.md' }
        - { path: 'package.json' }
    enforce: block
  - id: no-secrets-in-commits
    scope: ci
    when: { diff_regex: '(?i)(aws_secret_access_key|ghp_|sk-[a-z0-9]{20,})' }
    enforce: fail`;
---
<Base>
  <section class="hero-gradient">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-20 pb-16 text-center">
      <span class="badge mb-5">v0.1.3 · open source</span>
      <h1 class="text-5xl sm:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-[1.05]">
        Make your coding agents <span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-primary-400 to-emerald-300 bg-clip-text text-transparent">obey the rules</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-300">
        One <code class="rounded bg-white/5 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm font-mono text-primary-200">.policyctl.yml</code> file, enforced everywhere your code is written — Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and your CI. No more hand-written migrations, no more secrets in commits, no more "the agent just did it."
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@policyctl/cli" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          npm i -g @policyctl/cli
        </a>
        <a class="btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/RavaniRoshan/policyctl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          View on GitHub
        </a>
        <a class="btn-ghost" href="/docs">Read the docs</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-6 text-xs text-slate-500">
        Free · MIT · works in any repo
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16">
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="text-primary-300 text-sm font-medium mb-2">In real time</div>
        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Hooks fire on every tool call — block the bad action at the door, before it touches your repo.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="text-primary-300 text-sm font-medium mb-2">In CI</div>
        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The same policy gates the git diff in CI. Catches what hooks miss — including human PRs.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="text-primary-300 text-sm font-medium mb-2">Across agents</div>
        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          One policy file. Wire it into Claude Code, Codex, or Cursor in one command. No per-model plugins.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="how-it-works" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How it works</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-slate-300 max-w-2xl">Three commands, one file. No backend required for the CLI; a hosted control plane is optional.</p>

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500">01</div>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold">Init</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Scaffold a starter policy from a template.</p>
        <pre class="code-block mt-4"><code>policyctl init --template full</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500">02</div>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold">Wire</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Generate provider hook glue for Claude, Codex, or Cursor.</p>
        <pre class="code-block mt-4"><code>policyctl gen claude
policyctl gen codex
policyctl gen cursor</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500">03</div>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold">Check</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Gate the diff in CI. Get a full violation feed in the dashboard.</p>
        <pre class="code-block mt-4"><code>policyctl check
policyctl check --report</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What you can enforce</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-slate-300 max-w-2xl">A rule is a matcher set, an enforce level, and a scope. Compose them. Allowlist reviewed exceptions. Tag them.</p>
    <div class="code-block mt-6 overflow-x-auto"><code>{example}</code></div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Commands</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="card py-4"><div class="font-mono text-sm text-primary-300">init</div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Scaffold a .policyctl.yml from a template.</p></div>
      <div class="card py-4"><div class="font-mono text-sm text-primary-300">list</div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Show loaded rules and their scope.</p></div>
      <div class="card py-4"><div class="font-mono text-sm text-primary-300">check</div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Run the CI/diff gate. Non-zero on violation.</p></div>
      <div class="card py-4"><div class="font-mono text-sm text-primary-300">eval</div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Run the hook evaluator (reads JSON on stdin).</p></div>
      <div class="card py-4"><div class="font-mono text-sm text-primary-300">gen</div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Generate Claude / Codex / Cursor hook glue.</p></div>
      <div class="card py-4"><div class="font-mono text-sm text-primary-300">doctor</div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Verify hooks are wired correctly.</p></div>
      <div class="card py-4"><div class="font-mono text-sm text-primary-300">trace</div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Explain which matchers fire for a given input.</p></div>
      <div class="card py-4"><div class="font-mono text-sm text-primary-300">test</div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Run the policy against a fixture suite.</p></div>
      <div class="card py-4"><div class="font-mono text-sm text-primary-300">login / push / pull</div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Optional hosted control plane (org policy sync).</p></div>
      <div class="card py-4"><div class="font-mono text-sm text-primary-300">report</div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-400">Send a violation result to the hosted feed.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Stop shipping agent accidents.</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-slate-300">One file, every agent, every repo. Free forever for the CLI.</p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
      <a class="btn-primary" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@policyctl/cli" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        Install policyctl
      </a>
      <a class="btn-ghost" href="/docs">Read the docs</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
